{"event_type":"review","id":"e5174e99ae7ebf28443675eb9928352f8d593e51bc68c9910050bb2b2b7a2656","occurred_at":"2026-11-17T04:53:02Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/79715869b495ddf48520d4896a66c1f93f77f9939ddcd9735430500226c4a66b","sha256":"79715869b495ddf48520d4896a66c1f93f77f9939ddcd9735430500226c4a66b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a8d64ce269dad83b9bd501b88e54be80de2c73aee182cd4bacb339dc4b665b21","sha256":"a8d64ce269dad83b9bd501b88e54be80de2c73aee182cd4bacb339dc4b665b21"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/37ba51c076e4ee279ae0a0dea5dc036251967ffb657c1c54ae5153b1c355a457","sha256":"37ba51c076e4ee279ae0a0dea5dc036251967ffb657c1c54ae5153b1c355a457"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c0e79f1a190e65ee52c7fb98a97cb8cb42f98e98bc450ce0bf8040b0d8d03e79","sha256":"c0e79f1a190e65ee52c7fb98a97cb8cb42f98e98bc450ce0bf8040b0d8d03e79"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5cf8f263cac2176746d69bf8ea40c0a20ce19e004a261599a4d7184687af57ca","sha256":"5cf8f263cac2176746d69bf8ea40c0a20ce19e004a261599a4d7184687af57ca"}],"attempt_id":"9f317c301d31eab6c23e5101bd5e4200790e44825a19da36f570dff30b1cab73:0:2","base":"d381cadf1c31269e6d6e1791e34391b6c30d6e3e","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"150d3e6d3ef595f6675d9e201150bbd183364e7d","body":"**Keep the reviewed head on the body-only retry.**\n\nThe retry at `src/policy/crq/prReviewFindings.ts:1441` passes `hunks=null`, so Line 1047 removes `commit_id`. If the PR advances from A to B before that retry, GitHub associates the review with B, although its findings and reviewed-range text describe A. GitHub defaults an omitted `commit_id` to the most recent PR commit. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/pulls/reviews))\n\nSet `commit_id` independently of inline-hunk availability. If GitHub cannot accept the reviewed commit, report the failure instead of attaching its review to another commit.","id":"01237880ba370a14780868150d161810f7565071d0f3905a7b743b7937c5d508","intervals":[[1047,1047]],"path":"src/policy/crq/prReviewFindings.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep the reviewed head on the body-only retry."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"f793f23f537c2bae5a9a50d473fc347e290f9569","body":"**Make harvest replay idempotent before the retry count changes the action.**\n\n`planRepairHarvest` accepts a row with no `receipt.repair_task`. After a `needs-retriage` write, the row points at the new event. If the same harvested outcome is planned again from that updated row, the new event counts toward `maxFindingRetries`. The action then becomes `needs-human`, which changes the source key. The retained-event check does not match the original outcome, so a second `finding-event` is written. The callers do not reject rows without a receipt or rows already in a terminal state before planning.\n\nMake the replay check independent of the escalated action, or exclude the outcome the row already records from the retry count. Keep the retry bound for distinct failures.","id":"df04e2fe4b457d18fbabe4f24808d04b46180b4c9e5035a8024132f6c5b0f54b","intervals":[[300,304]],"path":"src/policy/crq/repairHarvest.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Make harvest replay idempotent before the retry count changes the action."}],"head":"ec59ffab5f1ea45d3c9a19a8ff37e231a5a996e9","head_tree":"12e1095fbecea104e28eb07c86b1760f1f72bd77","input_scope":[{"blob":"150d3e6d3ef595f6675d9e201150bbd183364e7d","intervals":[[1,1642]],"path":"src/policy/crq/prReviewFindings.ts"},{"blob":"f793f23f537c2bae5a9a50d473fc347e290f9569","intervals":[[1,348]],"path":"src/policy/crq/repairHarvest.ts"}],"job_id":"9f317c301d31eab6c23e5101bd5e4200790e44825